<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peene</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peene is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecklenburg-vorpommern">Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania</a>, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, about 100 km long. It flows east through Demmin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anklam">Anklam</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szczecin">Szczecin</a> Lagoon, and its name is also given to the Peenestrom channel separating the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usedom">Usedom</a> from the mainland. It long marked a boundary in medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> and later between Swedish and Prussian Pomerania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peene.jpg" alt="Peene" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Botaurus stellaris · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peene-VI-2007-352.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
